{"name":"Two Harbours","hex":"#bed3e1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"two","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO & ICAO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the digit 2."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tswapong."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/two"},{"term":"harbours","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of harbour"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of harbour"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harbours"}],"entries":[{"title":"Two Harbors, California","blocks":[{"text":"Two Harbors, colloquially known as \"The Isthmus\", is a small unincorporated community island village on the island of Santa Catalina Island, California, United States, with a population of 298. It is the second center of population on the island, besides the city of Avalon. It is mainly a resort village. It has only one restaurant, one hotel and one general store. The village has about 150 permanent residents who live on the isthmus year-round. One notable feature was the one-room schoolhouse which closed in 2014."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Two_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/330px-Two_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_Harbors%2C_California"},{"title":"Two Harbors, Minnesota","blocks":[{"text":"Two Harbors is a city and the county seat of Lake County, Minnesota, United States, along the shore of Lake Superior. The population was 3,633 at the 2020 census. Minnesota State Highway 61 serves as a main route in Two Harbors. Gooseberry Falls State Park is 13 miles (21 km) to the northeast. The city is home to a cargo shipping port for mined iron ore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Two_Harbors_Minnesota_aerial_view.jpg/330px-Two_Harbors_Minnesota_aerial_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_Harbors%2C_Minnesota"},{"title":"Harbor","blocks":[{"text":"A harbor or harbour is a sheltered part of a body of water where ships, boats, and barges can be moored."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Jebel_Ali_Port_2_Imresolt.jpg/330px-Jebel_Ali_Port_2_Imresolt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harbor"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Two_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-Two_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Two_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/1280px-Two_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Two_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-Two_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_Harbors_Catalina_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Two_Harbors_Isthmus%2C_Santa_Catalina_Island.jpg/500px-Two_Harbors_Isthmus%2C_Santa_Catalina_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Two_Harbors_Isthmus%2C_Santa_Catalina_Island.jpg/1280px-Two_Harbors_Isthmus%2C_Santa_Catalina_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/